      "description": "Watch Barcelona vs Racing Santander highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. The La Liga clash on September 16, 2026, between Barcelona and Racing Santander promised high drama as both teams looked to assert their dominance in the league standings. Fans at the stadium were treated to an exhibition of attacking football that shifted momentum rapidly throughout the evening. Early Pressure and Quick Returns Barcelona clinical nature was evident from the opening whistle, as they monopolized possession and forced Racing Santander deep into their own half. The breakthrough arrived in the 8th minute when Joao Cancelo unleashed a brilliant strike from outside the box, assisted by the young maestro Lamine Yamal . The pressure intensified, leading to a 25th-minute penalty after a VAR review confirmed a foul by Pedro Felipe on Raphinha . The Brazilian attacker stepped up and coolly slotted the ball home to double the lead, leaving goalkeeper Julen Agirrezabala with no chance. A Seesaw Battle Before the Break Despite the deficit, Racing Santander showed resilience. In the 30th minute, Maguette Gueye found the back of the net after a clever setup by Asier Villalibre , briefly silencing the home crowd. However, the momentum swung back to the hosts in the 36th minute when Villalibre inadvertently turned the ball into his own net during a defensive scramble. Barcelona capitalized on this fortune, and in the 42nd minute, Raphinha bagged his second goal of the match following a precise key pass from Dani Olmo . The first half concluded with further drama as Lamine Yamal saw his penalty attempt saved by a defiant Agirrezabala . Raphinha’s Hat-trick and the Final Flourish The second half continued the high-octane narrative. While Racing Santander pulled another goal back in the 65th minute through Yassir Zabiri following a lapse from Wojciech Szczesny , Barcelona response was immediate and devastating. Raphinha completed his hat-trick from the penalty spot just two minutes later after Karim Adeyemi was tripped in the area. The substitutions further boosted the home side's energy, with Gabriel Jesus finding the net in the 79th minute. Finally, in the 89th minute, Lamine Yamal added his name to the scoresheet with a clinical left-footed finish, cementing a dominant victory characterized by nearly 70% ball possession."
